LibreChat for multi-user access with API keys and HTTPS termination via Apache. The setup targets

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:22.720
fewer than 10 concurrent users and highlights current concurrency limits in law-moss swap.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:28.580
Teams needing simple self-hosted multi-tenant inference can adapt the described proxy

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:34.220
and key management pattern. Okay, let's pop the hood on the network side of pre-fill decode

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:40.560
disaggregation. Everyone treats pre-fill decode disaggregation as a simple split that just needs more

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:47.900
GPUs. In practice, the KV cache handoff between pre-fill and decode nodes creates highly directional

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:54.480
bursty traffic that standard fat tree or rail optimized apologies were never designed to carry.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:08:01.320
The pre-fill side generates large, contiguous KV blocks that must cross the network in a short window.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:06.480
Decode nodes request smaller, latency-sensitive slices on different schedules.

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:13.160
This mismatch produces leaf switch hotspots and PFC backpressure even when aggregate bandwidth

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:20.220
looks sufficient. Zai's flattened bipartite design removes the spine layer entirely, so every

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:26.000
leaf pair has a direct path. It eliminates the static rail mapping that forces traffic through

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:33.960
congested spines. The 33% hardware cost reduction and 40% tail latency improvement come directly from

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:40.220
removing those forced hops rather than adding more bandwidth. When your decode cluster is larger than

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:46.820
your pre-fill cluster or when context lengths vary widely, the topology choice matters more than raw

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:54.160
switch speed. The practical test is whether your first token P99 stays flat as you scale the decode pool.

00:08:54.780 --> 00:09:00.740
If it climbs, the network mapping is the next place to look. Run the perplexity unigram tokenizer

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:05.880
in a ranker pipeline to measure the reported five times latency drop on your workload.

